# Auto-use required plugins

For every task, proactively use the relevant plugins/MCP tools — do not wait for the user to ask. Authenticate with `mcp_auth` if a server is `needsAuth`. Prefer live MCP data over guessing.

## When to use which plugin

| Task / signal | Plugin / MCP |
|---------------|--------------|
| Firebase Auth, FCM, Analytics, `firebase.js`, `VITE_FIREBASE_*`, `.firebaserc` | **Firebase** — project/apps/config/rules/docs |
| MongoDB, Mongoose, collections, Atlas, DB queries | **MongoDB** |
| Sentry, production errors, `sentry.js`, crash reports | **Sentry** (Seer when debugging issues) |
| Deploy, hosting, env vars, Next/Vercel | **Vercel** skills / MCP if available |
| Railway deploy, services, logs, infra | **Railway** (MCP or CLI) |
| Library/API “how does X work?” docs | **Context7** |
| UI verify, click flows, screenshots | **Browse** / Cursor Browser |
| Git, PRs, issues, branches | **GitLens / GitKraken** |
| Models, datasets, Spaces, HF Hub | **Hugging Face** |
| Image/video/audio generation | **Higgsfield** |
| Persistent user/agent memory | **Mem0** (if ready) |
| Figma designs → code | **Figma** |

## CrwdCtrl defaults

- Auth / push / Firebase config → Firebase first.
- Backend data → MongoDB when the code or task touches the DB.
- “Why is prod broken?” → Sentry before guessing.
- Docs for npm packages → Context7 before outdated training knowledge.
- “Does this UI work?” → Browser tools.

## Rules of engagement

1. Call only plugins that match the task — not every plugin every time.
2. If a needed MCP is `error`/`needsAuth`, try auth/reconnect once; then continue with CLI/skills and note the blocker briefly.
3. Use official plugin skills when present (Firebase, Railway, Sentry, Vercel, etc.).
4. Never invent project IDs, issue IDs, or deploy status — fetch via MCP/CLI.
